---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>{SITE.title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={SITE.description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={SITE.title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={SITE.description} />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content={SITE.title} />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={SITE.title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={SITE.description} />
    <SharedHead />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div
      class="min-h-screen bg-black text-white overflow-x-hidden px-4 py-12 sm:px-8 sm:py-16 font-display flex items-center justify-center"
    >
      <main class="max-w-3xl w-full space-y-4 sm:space-y-6">
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          Hi! This is the
          <span class="line-through">wonderfully designed</span>
          website of Johnston Liu. I'm from Vancouver, Canada, and I'm a machine
          learning engineer at Suno based in Cambridge, MA. I stare & listen to
          data, read claude, and make gpus do things. I'm a graduate of the
          University of Chicago with a double major in Mathematics and Computer
          Science.
        </p>

        <p class={bodyClass}>
          Prior to moving to machine learning, I worked on our infrastructure
          team. I spent my time on:
        </p>
        <ol
          class={`list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 marker:text-neutral-400 ${bodyClass}`}
        >
          <li>
            On-call incident triage and Slack engineering agents (credentialless
            sandbox w/ bash + cli tools, integrated with existing company
            tooling, harness-outside-sandbox runtime and Durable Object-style
            SQLite WAL / S3 state).
          </li>
          <li>
            Kubernetes sandbox platform (gVisor isolation, Cilium and Envoy
            egress controls + credential injection, ~1s cold starts via node
            image prepulling, warm node buffers, and a node-local CSI git
            cache).
          </li>
          <li>
            Persistent Cloud Hypervisor microVM devboxes (Tailscale,
            checkpoint/restore migration, live-swappable VM runner upgrades,
            memory hot-plug, and live resizing).
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p class={bodyClass}>
          Before all of this, I worked in the Bay Area at Pure Storage on the
          FlashBlade kernel team getting kernel modules and hardware devices to
          work. I also built an
          <a href="https://docs.johnstonliu.me/ai-wrappers" class={linkClass}
            >AI Agent</a
          >
          (maybe at some point i'll write this, but quickly became obsolete).
          Before that, I was in NYC at CMS Holdings performing research into
          trading strategies and building research tools in Python. And even
          before that, I did mathematics research on symmetric monoidal
          preorders and their applications to finite topological spaces. The
          relevant paper (archaic at this point) can be found{" "}
          <a href="/documents/reu_paper.pdf" class={linkClass}>here</a>. If
          you'd like to contact me, feel free to use any of the links below!
        </p>

        <nav
          class="pt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-4 gap-y-3 text-base sm:gap-x-8 sm:text-lg"
        >
          {contactLinks.map(({ href, label, iconWidth, iconPath }) => (
            <a
              href={href}
              class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 relative group inline-flex items-center gap-2"
            >
              <svg
                class="h-[1em] w-[1.25em] overflow-visible"
                viewBox={`0 0 ${iconWidth} 512`}
                fill="currentColor"
                aria-hidden="true"
                focusable="false"
              >
                <path d={iconPath} />
              </svg>
              {label}
              <span class="absolute -bottom-1 left-0 w-0 h-0.5 bg-blue-400 group-hover:w-full transition-all duration-300" />
            </a>
          ))}
        </nav>

        <footer
          class="pt-4 sm:pt-6 text-center text-gray-400 text-sm sm:text-base"
        >
          <p>Last Updated 11/21/2026</p>
        </footer>
      </main>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
